// A function whose body is one large list literal of records is built entirely in the function's stack
// frame on the ESP32-S3 target: with 400 four-field records the frame is about 77 KB, over the Xtensa
// `entry` limit of 32,760 bytes, so the assembler rejects the function (board actor stacks are far smaller
// anyway). Found 2026-10-05 while generating a device description with ~400 register rows. The Mac and
// Linux emitters tolerate the frame. Expected on every target: prints 400, 1596, 4 and 0, exits 0.
// Once fixed, large list literals must be built on the heap (or otherwise not in one frame).

use trial_support_int64;

